n":"stop","timestamp":1784950337951,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ff0defae-2bae-4499-921e-2db70b801f05","responseModel":"Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507"}},"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Test List\n\nTest List Created:\n**Feature**: Claim Office Policy Management\n**Test File**: src/claim-office.spec.ts\n**Tests**: 29\n\n**Test Cases** (ordered simple -> complex):\n1. should return premium of 5 G for empty item list -- covers 'empty item list → premium 5 G'\n2. should reject quote with unknown item type with non-zero exit code -- covers 'quote includes an item with an unknown type'\n3. should reject claim with damage to item not in policy with non-zero exit code -- covers 'claim references a damage entry whose item is not part of the policy'\n4. should reject claim with negative damage amount with non-zero exit code -- covers 'claim contains a damage entry with amount: -200'\n5. should calculate base premium 100 G for a sword -- from MHPCO price list\n6. should calculate base premium 60 G for an amulet -- from MHPCO price list\n7. should calculate base premium 80 G for a staff -- from MHPCO price list\n8. should calculate base premium 40 G for a potion -- from MHPCO price list\n9. should calculate base premium 25 G per component for runes and moonstones -- from MHPCO price list\n10. should apply 60 G base premium for a building block of exactly 3 alike components -- covers '3 runes → 60 G base premium'\n11. should not apply block discount for 4 alike components -- covers '4 runes → 100 G base premium'\n12. should not apply block discount for different types of components -- covers '2 runes + 1 moonstone → 75 G base premium'\n13. should apply separate blocks for 3 runes and 3 moonstones totaling 120 G -- covers '3 runes + 3 moonstones → 120 G base premium'\n14. should add 50% risk surcharge for cursed items to the item's base premium -- e.g., cursed sword base premium 100 G + 50 G = 150 G\n15. should add 30% risk surcharge for highly enchanted items (enchantment ≥ 5) to the item's base premium -- e.g., enchanted sword with enchantment 5: 100 G + 30 G = 130 G\n16. should apply 20% loyalty discount to policy base premium for customers with ≥ 2 years with MHPCO -- from integration example\n17. should add 10% initial assessment surcharge for first insurance to the policy base premium -- from integration example\n18. should apply 15% discount on each contract after the first to the policy base premium -- from integration example\n19. should add 5 G processing fee to every premium at the very end -- from rules\n20. should process newcomer with a cursed sword to return premium of 165 G -- integration example: 100 + 50 + 10 + 5 = 165\n21. should process long-standing customer's second contract with cursed, enchanted sword to return premium of 160 G -- integration example: 100 + 50 + 30 - 20 + 10 - 15 + 5 = 160\n22. should apply rounding up for final premium (e.g., 197.5 G → 198 G) -- in MHPCO's favor\n23. should apply rounding down for final payout (e.g., 350.5 G → 350 G) -- in MHPCO's favor\n24. should apply 100 G deductible per damage event -- e.g., damage 500 G → payout 400 G\n25. should apply 50% reimbursement for damage to items with enchantment level ≥ 8 -- e.g., damage 1000 G → payout 500 G before deductible\n26. should fully reimburse damage to items made of dragon material -- e.g., damage 800 G → payout 800 G before deductible\n27. should apply capped payout if both dragon material and high enchantment clauses apply, with high enchantment winning -- e.g., dragon sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → payout 400 G\n28. should fully reimburse dragon material sword with enchantment 5, damage 800 G → payout 700 G\n29. should reimburse steel sword with enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → payout 400 G\n3"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"nebius/qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output