00 G before deductible\n27. should apply capped payout if both dragon material and high enchantment clauses apply, with high enchantment winning -- e.g., dragon sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → payout 400 G\n28. should fully reimburse dragon material sword with enchantment 5, damage 800 G → payout 700 G\n29. should reimburse steel sword with enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → payout 400 G\n30. should reject claim with more damage entries than insured items of that type -- multiple items of the same type rule\n31. should calculate insurance sum as sum of items' insurance values, with cap at twice the sum -- e.g., sword and amulet: sum 1600 G, cap 3200 G\n32. should base claim cap on unmodified insurance value, ignoring premium modifiers -- e.g., cursed sword insurance value 1000 G → cap 2000 G\n33. should consider block discount only for premium, not for insurance sum -- e.g., sword and 3 runes: insurance sum 1750 G\n34. should reduce payout if remaining cap"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"nebius/qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784950337951,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ff0defae-2bae-4499-921e-2db70b801f05","responseModel":"Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507"}}
