ap 3200 G\n32. should base claim cap on unmodified insurance value, ignoring premium modifiers -- e.g., cursed sword insurance value 1000 G → cap 2000 G\n33. should consider block discount only for premium, not for insurance sum -- e.g., sword and 3 runes: insurance sum 1750 G\n34. should reduce payout if remaining cap is less than calculated payout -- first claim reduces cap, second claim pays remaining cap\n\n**Next"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"nebius/qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784950337951,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ff0defae-2bae-4499-921e-2db70b801f05","responseModel":"Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507"}},"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Test List\n\nTest List Created:\n**Feature**: Claim Office Policy Management\n**Test File**: src/claim-office.spec.ts\n**Tests**: 29\n\n**Test Cases** (ordered simple -> complex):\n1. should return premium of 5 G for empty item list -- covers 'empty item list → premium 5 G'\n2. should reject quote with unknown item type with non-zero exit code -- covers 'quote includes an item with an unknown type'\n3. should reject claim with damage to item not in policy with non-zero exit code -- covers 'claim references a damage entry whose item is not part of the policy'\n4. should reject claim with negative damage amount with non-zero exit code -- covers 'claim contains a damage entry with amount: -200'\n5. should calculate base premium 100 G for a sword -- from MHPCO price list\n6. should calculate base premium 60 G for an amulet -- from MHPCO price list\n7. should calculate base premium 80 G for a staff -- from MHPCO price list\n8. should calculate base premium 40 G for a potion -- from MHPCO price list\n9. should calculate base premium 25 G per component for runes and moonstones -- from MHP